Carroll,

I have made the last set of edits you gave me.  A few minor
points.

  1) The DEX MEAN and DEX SD plots are not limited to 2 levels
     per factor.

  2) I left in the discussion about how relative histograms
     are normalized.  This discussion is not Dataplot specific.
     Although most packages probably do it one or the other,
     it is actually relevant to know which way they do it and
     to understand that there actually is a difference.

  3) Will does not currently have a page on the correlation
     coefficient.  I talked to him about this and he seemed
     willing to add it.  If and when he does, I will activate
     these links.

  4) There is currently no explicit discussion in any of the
     pages about the central limit thereom.  An appropriate
     place might be in the gallery of probability distributions
     under the normal distribution page.

  5) There is currently no 2-sample chi-square or 2-sample K-S
     test pages to link to.  I could either add these pages
     in the quantitative techniques section or delete reference
     to them altogether.

Alan
